//! expect-check-fail: 'whole' is moved while 'tag' still views it
//! expect-check-fail: = help: `tag` is in scope until its block ends: read what you need from it in a scope that ends before the move (for a pattern binding, a `match` on a borrow of the value), then move `whole`

// §9.7, §21.1: inside `whole @ .Click(tag, n)` a `tag` that is not Copy is
// a view of `whole`. Moving `whole` while `tag` is in scope is refused, as
// for any view. It compiled, and `tag` had been moved out of `whole`, which
// then held a blank.
type Tag { name: str }
impl Drop for Tag:
    move fn drop(): print(f"drop {self.name}")

enum Ev:
    Click(tag: Tag, n: i32)

fn take(e: Ev) -> i32:
    match move e:
        .Click(t, n) => n + t.name.len() as i32

fn handle(e: Ev) -> i32:
    match move e:
        whole @ .Click(tag, n) => tag.name.len() as i32 + take(whole)

fn main:
    print(handle(.Click(Tag { name: "a" }, 9)))
